```{r setup}
library(LIsing)
```

### Network Estimation

The following chunk of code simulates a dataset containing presence/absence information for 50 subjects taken over 4 time points.

```{r}
n <- 200; p <- 10
X <- matrix(data = NA, nrow = n, ncol = p + 3)
colnames(X) <- c("ID", "Measure", "Time", paste0("M", 1:p))

X[,"ID"] <- rep(1:50, each = 4)
X[,"Measure"] <- rep(c(1:4), 50)
X[,"Time"] <- X[,"Measure"]

X[,-c(1:3)] <- rbernoulli(n = n*p, p = 0.5)
head(X)
```

The following chunk of code estimates the network from this using the nodewise regression approach.

```{r}
theta.res <- estimate.parameters.nw(X = X, theta.init = NULL, tau.init = 0.5, penalty = "1se", symm = "min")
print(theta.res)
```
The following chunk of code estimates the network from this using the joint approach.


```{r}
theta.res <- estimate.parameters.j(X = X, theta.init = NULL, tau.init = 0.5, penalty = "1se")
print(theta.res)
```





